{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 10A Problems/Problem 6\">2021 Fall AMC 10A #6</a> and <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">2021 Fall AMC 12A #5</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(Simple_and_Quick)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (Simple and Quick)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_HS_Competition_Academy\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by HS Competition Academy</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Elmer the emu takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b45828f292e161290be6ee62bc4c9df081ee1e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> equal strides to walk between consecutive telephone poles on a rural road. Oscar the ostrich can cover the same distance in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> equal leaps. The telephone poles are evenly spaced, and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba6cdde56f366d628a7a35826f98523dbe58bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />st pole along this road is exactly one mile (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/c/2fc92cb8cdff39ca4dac9ec6fb3224dbe5fa50a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5280$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> feet) from the first pole. How much longer, in feet, is Oscar's leap than Elmer's stride?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/9/489aafa0575fabf6ab2d6d9a5981ddc477b4c7a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }6\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }8\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }10\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }11\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"382\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9b2cca3677e5e007bf4bc97b8259849aac5a431.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41-1=40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> gaps between the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba6cdde56f366d628a7a35826f98523dbe58bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> telephone poles, so the distance of each gap is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f90896563118550cc5c6b7c03d6937e92c36d351.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5280\\div40=132$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"130\" height=\"15\" /> feet.\n</p><p>Each of Oscar's leaps covers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/e/e7edd5e21655daf31b5cd7acbc516aba4d890506.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$132\\div12=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" /> feet, and each of Elmer's strides covers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d43b80d9a830fdbc43fa5f1d3c9e2a851a9b94ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$132\\div44=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" /> feet.\n</p><p>Therefore, Oscar's leap is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e17a9232d0e33cf379c083c2872edd75a88c5808.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11-3=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"131\" height=\"30\" /> feet longer than Elmer's stride.\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/b/a9b2cca3677e5e007bf4bc97b8259849aac5a431.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41-1=40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" /> gaps between the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba6cdde56f366d628a7a35826f98523dbe58bd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$41$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> telephone poles, so Elmer takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/6/686b643694a60e82b60b1d319b38f4f690f3ace4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$44 \\cdot 40 = 1760$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" /> strides in total, and Oscar takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f19c18ea72d040066a8699aeaef52e5491ab99c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12 \\cdot 40 = 480$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"103\" height=\"14\" /> leaps in total. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/2/532d1d3773a4ec969d77f964191a8189f86d5efb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(5280 \\div 480) - (5280 \\div 1760) = 11-3=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"386\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~MrThinker\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28Simple_and_Quick.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(Simple_and_Quick)\">Video Solution (Simple and Quick)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (Simple and Quick)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/895dqtet8MA\">https://youtu.be/895dqtet8MA</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>for AMC 10: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ycRZHCOKTVk\">https://youtu.be/ycRZHCOKTVk</a>\n</p><p>for AMC 12: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/jY-17W6dA3c?t=591\">https://youtu.be/jY-17W6dA3c?t=591</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_WhyMath\">Video Solution by WhyMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by WhyMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/AEmEKsHe2i0\">https://youtu.be/AEmEKsHe2i0</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_HS_Competition_Academy\">Video Solution by HS Competition Academy</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by HS Competition Academy\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/0HjK-M6BJ8E\">https://youtu.be/0HjK-M6BJ8E</a>\n</p><p>~Charles3829\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/TjWjrApq-OQ\">https://youtu.be/TjWjrApq-OQ</a>\n</p><p>~Lucas\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A\">2021 Fall AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wik